### Describe the bug

When using `expect()` in a helper function within `waitFor()`, I want the error to show the line where the helper function was called, not the line in the helper function. Adding `vi.defineHelper` does not help in this case.

### Reproduction

```js
import { vi, test, expect } from "vitest";

const good = vi.defineHelper(
  async () => {
    expect(1).toBe(2)
  }
);
const bad = vi.defineHelper(
  async () => vi.waitFor(() => {
    expect(1).toBe(2)
  })
);

test("good", async () => {
  await good();
});
test("bad", async () => {
  await bad();
});
```

